    narr:narration """This narrative hub maintains the strategic positioning of the product as a [structured async decision platform](narr:Position_ProductCategoryAsyncPlatform), explicitly framed as a direct alternative to [real-time chat tools](narr:Position_AntiPatternRealtimeChat). The core market hypothesis, established in March 2026, focuses on [remote teams of 10-50 people](narr:Position_TargetMarketRemoteTeams) experiencing decision-loss. While the initial [pricing was established at $12/user/month](narr:Position_PricingTwelveDollars), the trajectory reveals a shift toward tiered complexity, with a March 2026 retro introducing a $15/user price point for larger teams. By August 2026, the narrative focus shifted toward validating this model through performance metrics, as seen in the [Sprint 4 success framing](narr:Position_Sprint4SuccessEvidenceFrame), which utilizes [team velocity](narr:Expr_1E2ETanyaCollab1786441387536_2) as a primary indicator of operational health.""" ;
